title scooter_paint -- a live conversation folded to pixels, GREEN
prompt Autonomous loop: read the road-ahead docs and REMEMBER, take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first optimizing for the balance compass, deep-read one council-rota doc, send often, stop at custody gates.
think Read REMEMBER's INNER LOOP live edge and the custody gates. The prior lap built image/text_grid.rye -- the abstract terminal-grid painter -- and its own recommend line named the next mechanical crux: the pond rung that feeds a live scooter_view.Frame's cells into render_grid, so the join built in the abstract becomes a real conversation painted. That is the balance-compass lap: it closes the loop between the terminal family and the open-media paint family on real data, rather than adding a twenty-first leaf font.
think Surveyed the two sides. scooter_view.Frame is a fixed 24x80 array of character cells (frame_rows*frame_cols = 1920 bytes), space-filled, produced by view.render(ch). text_grid.render_grid(allocator, atlas, cells, cols, rows, fg, bg) paints exactly that shape. The bridge is one call -- yet a Scooter post is member text, so a cell could carry a byte the 5x7 ASCII font cannot draw; text_grid would surface that as GridCellsMismatch downstream. The honest bridge adds a named gate: frame_is_paintable walks every cell, and paint_frame refuses ScooterFrameUnpaintable BY NAME before a pixel moves.
think Layering held right: pond composes image, never the reverse. scooter_paint.rye lives in pond/apps and imports DOWN into image/ (text_grid, font5x7_ascii, glyph, color, qoi). image/ stays self-contained.
think Build hitch, learned: rye resolves @import lexically against the importing file's symlink path, NOT the resolved real path. So a symlinked text_grid.rye in pond/apps could not find its own text_layout.rye -- the whole transitive image closure must be symlinked into pond/apps. Computed the closure by BFS (no python3 on the pier -- bash loop over grep) and seated twelve symlinks: text_grid, text_layout, text_paint, glyph, color, font5x7_ascii and its four corpora (alpha, lower, punct, symbol, font5x7), reusing the qoi and tally_copy symlinks already present. This matches the pattern photos.rye/sprite.rye already use.
think Witness crux -- faithful BY MEASURE: built a real 2-post channel (host opens, admits a member, ada and host each post), folded it to a Frame whose header reads "scooter: 2 posts" (a true journal, not a crafted grid), painted it, and proved the bridge is a pure pass-through -- render_channel's image is BYTE-FOR-BYTE what text_grid paints straight from the same cells. Then determinism (same channel, same image), a QOI round-trip byte-for-byte (the conversation is a real portable image), and the honest edge: poke one high byte into a copied frame and prove paint_frame refuses ScooterFrameUnpaintable, having painted nothing.
obs GREEN on the first metal run after the symlink closure was complete. tame_style_check bans clean (ratchet unchanged at 11 zero-assert files), width-check exit 0, both new files plain 7-bit ASCII. One early syntax slip -- wrote error.ScooterPaintError.ScooterFrameUnpaintable, corrected to the flat error.ScooterFrameUnpaintable before build.
obs Balance lap held: a bridge that JOINS the terminal and paint families on a REAL conversation, closing the loop the prior text_grid lap opened, rather than another font leaf -- the harmony compass over raw throughput. Correctly layered so image/ stays self-contained and pond reaches down.
obs Rota this lap (d27) deep-read item 19, context/KYRI.md -- the standing voice, the four faculties (Lattice's exact number, Scribble's open door, Lantern's honest mark of the proposed, Ember's earned craft). This rung is Lattice and Ember at work: every claim bound to a measured byte-for-byte identity, the making proven before it is called done.
loom witness=scooter_paint_witness channel_posts=2 frame=80x24 image_px=480x168 wall_ms=NA
